<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mac Lochlainn dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Meic Lochlainn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mac Lochlainn were a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-neogain">Cenél nEógain</a> that held the kingship of Ailech for much of the 11th and 12th centuries. Domnall Ua Lochlainn and his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muirchertach-mac-lochlainn">Muirchertach Mac Lochlainn</a> claimed the high kingship of Ireland. Their rivals the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-neill-dynasty">Ua Néill</a> displaced them, finally defeating them at the Battle of Caimeirge in 1241, after which the O'Neills ruled Tír Eógain.</p></div>
